// Spectraphon Side - Stories A + B + C + E
//   (single-side SAO + SAM analyzer + Array memory + Spectranoise Chaos/Noise)
//
// Single-side spectral oscillator with 64 harmonic partials split across an
// Odd bank (k = 1, 3, ..., 63) and an Even bank (k = 2, 4, ..., 64). Each
// bank is unrolled as 32 parallel sin_osc_ar voices summed together —
// klang_ar would require a 32+32-element signal array which exceeds Rhai's
// 16-arity limit, so the additive bank is unrolled per the plan §7 fallback.
//
// Story B — SAM analyzer:
//   When `sam_capture` selects a SAM mode, the per-partial magnitudes
//   come from a real-time FFT of the hardware audio input. The 2048-frame
//   FFT (Hann window, 50% hop) is read with `bin_data_kr` per partial,
//   one bin per harmonic centred on `k · f0_analyze · binsPerHz`.
//   Slide drives `f0_analyze` log-mapped to [50, 800] Hz (independent of
//   the oscillator pitch — see kb/spectraphon-synthdef-plan.md §3.d).
//   Each magnitude is smoothed with a 20 ms `lag_kr` (≈ 50 Hz one-pole)
//   to avoid zipper noise on bin updates.
//
//   DEVIATION from the kb plan §3.a `bandwidth_bins ∈ [1, 16]` design:
//   Focus does not modulate per-partial bandwidth in the analyser. Story
//   C's bilinear lookup already consumes 256 buf_rd UGens per side; a
//   bandwidth-3 kernel would push the SC synthdef definition message
//   past the 64 KB UDP limit (`Message too long`, errno 90, observed
//   while implementing Story B). Focus instead exclusively addresses
//   the Story C Array Y-axis. A wider bucket-sum is possible once the
//   synthdef framework moves to /d_recv + TCP or buffer-driven analysis.
//
//   DEVIATION from the ticket's literal "input parameter" requirement:
//   Rhai synthdef bodies cap at 10 params (vibelang-dsp/builder.rs) and
//   we are already at the cap, so the analyser pins itself to hardware
//   audio input ch 0 via `sound_in_ar`. To analyse an internal vibelang
//   bus, swap that line for `in_ar(<bus>, 1)` locally.
//
//   In SAM modes, Sub/CV (right_mode = 2) is replaced by an envelope
//   follower (`amplitude_ar`) on the analyser input per the plan §3.c.
//
// Story C — Array memory:
//   16 stored Arrays per side, each addressed by a 2-D Slide × Focus grid
//   of N_GRID × N_GRID cells holding 64 partial magnitudes. Total buffer is
//   N_ARRAYS × N_GRID × N_GRID × N_PARTIALS = 16 × 8 × 8 × 64 = 65536 floats.
//
//   SAM mode (sam_capture ≥ 1): partial magnitudes come from `mag_sam`.
//     When `sam_capture == 2` (capture active), mag_sam is written into
//     the cell `[array_idx, floor(slide·N_GRID), floor(focus·N_GRID), k-1]`
//     via a phase-offset gating trick on buf_wr_kr.
//
//   SAO mode (sam_capture == 0): partial magnitudes are read back from
//     the buffer using bilinear interpolation across the 4 cells around
//     the current (slide, focus). 4 buf_rd_kr per partial × 64 partials =
//     256 lookups per side at kr rate.
//
//   DEVIATION (documented for Story C follow-up): vibelang has no script-
//   level top-level buffer API yet (see kb/spectraphon-synthdef-plan.md
//   §6.C3). This story uses local_buf_ir, which is per-synth and does NOT
//   survive synthdef recompile — captured Arrays reset on hot-reload. A
//   future ticket should add `allocate_buffer(frames, channels)` to
//   vibelang-rhai and switch this synthdef to accept a `array_buf` bufnum
//   parameter pointing at a script-allocated buffer. Default-preset baking
//   (Array 0 = saw, 1 = square, 2 = noise) is also deferred to that ticket
//   since `set_buf_ir` cannot fan out to 65536 cells in one call.
//
// Story E — Spectranoise modes (Chaos + Noise) per kb plan §6.E and §4:
//
//   Chaos (mode=2): paired sines per side. Carrier_a = sin_osc_ar(freq);
//     carrier_b = sin_osc_ar(freq * chaos_ratio) where chaos_ratio is
//     focus-mapped to [1, 4]. `slide` drives chaos feedback through
//     fb_sine_l_ar (linear-interpolating chaotic sine, im + fb scale with
//     slide). `partials` becomes audio-rate AM depth — at partials=0 the
//     pair is clean; at partials=1 each carrier is fully AM-modulated by
//     the chaos voice. merge_even still folds carrier_b into the L jack.
//
//   Noise (mode=3): pink_noise_ar → lpf_ar(slide_cut) → hpf_ar(focus_cut)
//     → AM with sine carriers. slide_cut log-mapped 100..16000 Hz, focus_cut
//     log-mapped 20..2000 Hz. L jack gets bp * sin(f0); R jack gets
//     bp * sin(2*f0). merge_even folds the 2*f0 carrier into L like SAM/SAO.
//     `partials` is unused in Noise (the AM is intrinsic to the mode).
//     `right_mode` is also ignored in Chaos and Noise — those modes have
//     fixed L=Odd-equivalent / R=Even-equivalent topologies.
//
// `sam_capture` decode (extended for Story E — see kb plan §6.E3):
//   0 → SAO playback        (bank, sao_mix=1, no capture)
//   1 → SAM, no capture     (bank, sam_mix=1, no capture)
//   2 → Chaos               (paired sines + chaos feedback, partials = AM depth)
//   3 → Noise               (filtered pink-noise sidebands AM-modulating sines)
//   4 → SAM with capture    (bank, sam_mix=1, capture writes Story C array cell)
//
//   DEVIATION from the ticket's literal `mode=2 (Chaos), mode=3 (Noise)` and
//   the existing Story C encoding `2 = SAM + capture`: this synthdef keeps
//   parameter name `sam_capture` and its monotonic [0..N] integer encoding,
//   but renumbers SAM-with-capture from 2 → 4 to free values 2 and 3 for
//   Chaos and Noise per the ticket. Existing Story C patches that wrote
//   `sam_capture = 2` to engage capture must update to `sam_capture = 4`.
//   Param is folded mode+capture because the synthdef body is already at
//   the 10-argument Rhai cap (vibelang-dsp/builder.rs).
//
// Output convention (stereo channels mirror the hardware jacks):
//   L = Odd  jack — odd partials. With merge_even=1 (default), Even folds
//                   into Odd so unpatched-Even users hear all harmonics on L.
//   R = secondary jack:
//     SAO/SAM (mode 0/1/4): selected by `right_mode`:
//       right_mode = 0 (def) → Even jack: even bank (or odd if merge_even=1),
//                              gated by Partials like the hardware Even out.
//       right_mode = 1       → Sine jack: clean sin_osc_ar(freq) at k=1.
//                              Never gated by Partials — survives at partials=0.
//       right_mode = 2       → Sub/CV: SAO = saw_ar(freq * 0.5) * 0.5;
//                              SAM = amplitude_ar of the analyser input.
//     Chaos (mode 2): R = chaos_b (sin at freq*chaos_ratio) with AM.
//     Noise (mode 3): R = bp * sin(2*f0).
//
// Stories not yet integrated here: FM bus (Story D — see spectraphon_dual.vibe).
// See kb/spectraphon-synthdef-plan.md §3 (DSP arch), §4 (UGen mapping),
// §6.A (Story A), §6.B (Story B), §6.C (Story C), §6.E (Story E),
// §7 (storage format / risks).

define_synthdef("spectraphon_side", |builder| {
    builder
        .param("freq", 220.0)
        .param("partials", 1.0)
        .param("slide", 0.5)        // SAM: f0_analyze (log 50..800 Hz). SAO: Array X.
        .param("focus", 0.5)        // SAM: bucket-sum bandwidth weight. SAO: Array Y.
        .param("amp", 0.3)
        .param("gate", 1.0)
        .param("merge_even", 1.0)   // 1 = even folds into odd (mono); 0 = odd-L / even-R split
        .param("right_mode", 0.0)   // 0 = even-jack | 1 = sine | 2 = sub/CV
        .param("sam_capture", 1.0)  // mode: 0=SAO | 1=SAM | 2=Chaos | 3=Noise | 4=SAM+cap
        .param("array_idx", 0.0)    // 0..15 — which of the 16 stored Arrays to address
        .body(|freq, partials, slide, focus, amp, gate, merge_even, right_mode, sam_capture, array_idx| {

            let env = envelope()
                .asr(0.01, 1.0, 0.3)
                .gate(gate)
                .cleanup_on_finish()
                .build();

            // The per-partial gate g[k] = clamp(partials*N - (k-1), 0, 1)
            // reveals harmonics low-to-high as `partials` sweeps CCW → CW;
            // CCW (partials=0) → silent, CW (partials=1) → full spectrum.
            let n = 64.0;
            let scale = partials * n;

            // === Story B: SAM analyzer (FFT chain shared by all partials) ===
            // Hardware audio input ch 0 — see file header for the rationale.
            let analyze_in = sound_in_ar(0.0);
            // 2048-frame FFT, 50% hop, Hann window. Bin spacing at 44.1 kHz
            // is 21.5 Hz; the FFT writes magnitudes/phases into fft_buf and
            // bin_data_kr reads (mag, freq) per bin out of the active chain.
            let fft_buf = local_buf_ir(1.0, 2048.0);
            let chain = fft_kr(fft_buf, analyze_in, 0.5, 1.0, 1.0, 0.0);

            // Slide → analyser fundamental. Log-mapped 50..800 Hz so each
            // half-turn doubles the harmonic grid spacing (kb plan §3.d).
            let f0_analyze = 50.0 * pow(16.0, clip(slide, 0.0, 1.0));
            // Bin index per Hz at the assumed 44.1 kHz server rate.
            let bin_per_hz = 2048.0 / 44100.0;
            // Hann-windowed FFT magnitude scaling: a unit sine on a bin
            // produces ~N/4 ≈ 512, so 1/512 brings peaks back to ~1.0.
            let mag_scale = 0.001953125;
            // 60 dB lag time of 20 ms ≈ one-pole at ~55 Hz cutoff.
            let lag_t = 0.02;
            // Reusable Nyquist-safe bin clip range. Bin 0 is DC, bin 1024
            // is Nyquist for FFT size 2048; clamp reads to [1, 1023].
            let bin_max = 1023.0;

            // sam_capture decode (see file header for the truth table).
            // Monotonic one-hot via cumulative-clip differences:
            //   m_le_n = 1 when sam_capture ≤ n, else 0 (for integer values).
            // Each mode's mix coefficient is then the difference between
            // adjacent thresholds, yielding exactly one active coefficient
            // per integer mode value. cap_active is high only at mode=4.
            let m_le_0 = clip(1.0 - sam_capture, 0.0, 1.0);     // 1 at mode≤0
            let m_le_1 = clip(2.0 - sam_capture, 0.0, 1.0);     // 1 at mode≤1
            let m_le_2 = clip(3.0 - sam_capture, 0.0, 1.0);     // 1 at mode≤2
            let m_le_3 = clip(4.0 - sam_capture, 0.0, 1.0);     // 1 at mode≤3
            let sao_mix    = m_le_0;                             // mode=0
            let sam_only   = m_le_1 - m_le_0;                    // mode=1
            let chaos_mix  = m_le_2 - m_le_1;                    // mode=2
            let noise_mix  = m_le_3 - m_le_2;                    // mode=3
            let sam_cap    = 1.0 - m_le_3;                       // mode≥4
            let sam_mix    = sam_only + sam_cap;                 // SAM is mode 1 OR 4
            let cap_active = sam_cap;                            // capture only at mode=4

            // === Story C: shared 16-Array buffer + bilinear lookup ===
            //
            // Layout (flat 1D, row-major):
            //   idx = array_idx * (N_GRID * N_GRID * N_PARTIALS)
            //       + slide_cell * (N_GRID * N_PARTIALS)
            //       + focus_cell * N_PARTIALS
            //       + (k - 1)
            // Strides for N_GRID=8, N_PARTIALS=64:
            //   array_stride = 4096, row_stride = 512, cell_stride = 64.
            let array_buf = local_buf_ir(1, 65536.0);

            // Quantise slide/focus to grid cells. floor(x) = x - wrap(x,0,1)
            // since vibelang has no Floor UGen.
            let slide_pos = clip(slide, 0.0, 0.99999) * 8.0;
            let focus_pos = clip(focus, 0.0, 0.99999) * 8.0;
            let slide_lo = slide_pos - wrap_kr(slide_pos, 0.0, 1.0);
            let focus_lo = focus_pos - wrap_kr(focus_pos, 0.0, 1.0);
            let slide_hi = clip(slide_lo + 1.0, 0.0, 7.0);
            let focus_hi = clip(focus_lo + 1.0, 0.0, 7.0);
            let s_frac = slide_pos - slide_lo;
            let f_frac = focus_pos - focus_lo;

            // Bilinear weights — constant across all 64 partials in this kr cycle.
            let w00 = (1.0 - s_frac) * (1.0 - f_frac);
            let w01 = (1.0 - s_frac) * f_frac;
            let w10 = s_frac * (1.0 - f_frac);
            let w11 = s_frac * f_frac;

            let arr_base = clip(array_idx, 0.0, 15.0) * 4096.0;
            let base00 = arr_base + slide_lo * 512.0 + focus_lo * 64.0;
            let base01 = arr_base + slide_lo * 512.0 + focus_hi * 64.0;
            let base10 = arr_base + slide_hi * 512.0 + focus_lo * 64.0;
            let base11 = arr_base + slide_hi * 512.0 + focus_hi * 64.0;

            // Capture target = nearest (slide_lo, focus_lo) cell.
            // When capture is inactive we offset the write phase by 1e9 — far
            // past the 65536-frame buffer with loop=0, BufWr drops the write.
            let cap_base = arr_base + slide_lo * 512.0 + focus_lo * 64.0;
            let cap_offset = (1.0 - cap_active) * 1.0e9;

            // --- Odd bank: k = 1, 3, 5, ..., 63 ---------------------------
            let k = 1.0;
            let mag_sao = w00 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base00 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1)
                        + w01 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base01 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1)
                        + w10 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base10 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1)
                        + w11 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base11 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1);
            let centre_bin = clip(k * f0_analyze * bin_per_hz, 1.0, bin_max);
            let mag_centre = channels(bin_data_kr(chain, centre_bin, 0.5), 2)[0];
            let mag_sam = lag_kr(mag_centre * mag_scale, lag_t);
            buf_wr_kr(mag_sam, array_buf, cap_base + (k - 1.0) + cap_offset, 0);
            let mag_k = mag_sao * sao_mix + mag_sam * sam_mix;
            let odd_bank = sin_osc_ar(freq * k) * mag_k
                * clip(scale - (k - 1.0), 0.0, 1.0);
            for i in 1..32 {
                let k = (2 * i + 1).to_float();
                let mag_sao = w00 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base00 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1)
                            + w01 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base01 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1)
                            + w10 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base10 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1)
                            + w11 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base11 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1);
                let centre_bin = clip(k * f0_analyze * bin_per_hz, 1.0, bin_max);
                let mag_centre = channels(bin_data_kr(chain, centre_bin, 0.5), 2)[0];
                let mag_sam = lag_kr(mag_centre * mag_scale, lag_t);
                buf_wr_kr(mag_sam, array_buf, cap_base + (k - 1.0) + cap_offset, 0);
                let mag_k = mag_sao * sao_mix + mag_sam * sam_mix;
                odd_bank = odd_bank + sin_osc_ar(freq * k) * mag_k
                    * clip(scale - (k - 1.0), 0.0, 1.0);
            }

            // --- Even bank: k = 2, 4, 6, ..., 64 --------------------------
            let k = 2.0;
            let mag_sao = w00 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base00 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1)
                        + w01 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base01 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1)
                        + w10 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base10 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1)
                        + w11 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base11 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1);
            let centre_bin = clip(k * f0_analyze * bin_per_hz, 1.0, bin_max);
            let mag_centre = channels(bin_data_kr(chain, centre_bin, 0.5), 2)[0];
            let mag_sam = lag_kr(mag_centre * mag_scale, lag_t);
            buf_wr_kr(mag_sam, array_buf, cap_base + (k - 1.0) + cap_offset, 0);
            let mag_k = mag_sao * sao_mix + mag_sam * sam_mix;
            let even_bank = sin_osc_ar(freq * k) * mag_k
                * clip(scale - (k - 1.0), 0.0, 1.0);
            for i in 1..32 {
                let k = (2 * (i + 1)).to_float();
                let mag_sao = w00 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base00 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1)
                            + w01 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base01 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1)
                            + w10 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base10 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1)
                            + w11 * buf_rd_kr(1, array_buf, base11 + (k - 1.0), 0, 1);
                let centre_bin = clip(k * f0_analyze * bin_per_hz, 1.0, bin_max);
                let mag_centre = channels(bin_data_kr(chain, centre_bin, 0.5), 2)[0];
                let mag_sam = lag_kr(mag_centre * mag_scale, lag_t);
                buf_wr_kr(mag_sam, array_buf, cap_base + (k - 1.0) + cap_offset, 0);
                let mag_k = mag_sao * sao_mix + mag_sam * sam_mix;
                even_bank = even_bank + sin_osc_ar(freq * k) * mag_k
                    * clip(scale - (k - 1.0), 0.0, 1.0);
            }

            // Hardware "Even-into-Odd" normalization: when Even is unpatched
            // (merge_even = 1), even partials sum into the Odd jack and the
            // Even jack falls silent.
            let odd_out  = odd_bank + even_bank * merge_even;
            let even_out = even_bank * (1.0 - merge_even);

            // Bank L/R (SAO/SAM modes). default_right mirrors hardware Even
            // jack behaviour, gated by partials. sine/sub bypass the gate.
            let bank_left = odd_out;
            let default_right = (even_out * (1.0 - merge_even)
                                  + odd_out * merge_even) * partials;
            let sine_signal = sin_osc_ar(freq);
            let sub_sao = saw_ar(freq * 0.5) * 0.5;
            let sub_sam = amplitude_ar(analyze_in, 0.01, 0.1);
            let sub_signal = sub_sao * sao_mix + sub_sam * sam_mix;

            let active_default = 1.0 - clip(right_mode, 0.0, 1.0);
            let active_sub     = clip(right_mode - 1.0, 0.0, 1.0);
            let active_sine    = 1.0 - active_default - active_sub;

            let bank_right = default_right * active_default
                           + sine_signal   * active_sine
                           + sub_signal    * active_sub;

            // === Story E: Chaos mode (paired sines + chaos feedback) =====
            // chaos_ratio: focus → [1, 4], second-sine pitch ratio.
            // chaos_im / chaos_fb: slide drives index multiplier and feedback
            // amount of fb_sine_l_ar (linear-interpolating chaotic sine).
            // Defaults a=1.1, c=0.5, xi=yi=0.1 mirror the manifest defaults.
            let slide_c = clip(slide, 0.0, 1.0);
            let focus_c = clip(focus, 0.0, 1.0);
            let chaos_ratio = 1.0 + focus_c * 3.0;
            let chaos_im    = 0.5 + slide_c * 3.5;
            let chaos_fb    = slide_c * 0.5;
            let chaos_voice = fb_sine_l_ar(freq, chaos_im, chaos_fb,
                                            1.1, 0.5, 0.1, 0.1);
            let chaos_a = sine_signal;                  // reuse sin(freq)
            let chaos_b = sin_osc_ar(freq * chaos_ratio);
            // Audio-rate AM: at partials=0 the carriers are clean; at
            // partials=1 they are fully ring-modulated by the chaos voice.
            let chaos_am = 1.0 + chaos_voice * partials;
            let chaos_l_raw = (chaos_a + chaos_b * merge_even) * chaos_am * 0.5;
            let chaos_r_raw =  chaos_b * (1.0 - merge_even)    * chaos_am * 0.5;

            // === Story E: Noise mode (filtered pink-noise sidebands) =====
            // slide → LP cutoff (100..16000 Hz log); focus → HP cutoff
            // (20..2000 Hz log). bp = LPF then HPF — broad bandpass with
            // independent LP/HP corners. Carriers AM-modulate the noise.
            let slide_cut = lin_exp_kr(slide_c, 0.0, 1.0,    100.0, 16000.0);
            let focus_cut = lin_exp_kr(focus_c, 0.0, 1.0,     20.0,  2000.0);
            let noise_src = pink_noise_ar();
            let noise_lp  = lpf_ar(noise_src, slide_cut);
            let noise_bp  = hpf_ar(noise_lp,  focus_cut);
            let noise_car_odd  = sine_signal;             // sin(f0)   — odd
            let noise_car_even = sin_osc_ar(freq * 2.0);  // sin(2*f0) — even
            let noise_l_raw = noise_bp
                * (noise_car_odd + noise_car_even * merge_even) * 0.5;
            let noise_r_raw = noise_bp
                *  noise_car_even * (1.0 - merge_even)         * 0.5;

            // === Mode-mixed L/R ==========================================
            // Bank modes carry the existing global *partials VCA on L (SAO/SAM
            // hardware behaviour). Chaos folds partials in via AM depth, so
            // no global partials gate. Noise has no partials role at all.
            let bank_active = sao_mix + sam_mix;
            let left_raw  = bank_left  * bank_active * partials
                          + chaos_l_raw * chaos_mix
                          + noise_l_raw * noise_mix;
            let right_raw = bank_right * bank_active
                          + chaos_r_raw * chaos_mix
                          + noise_r_raw * noise_mix;

            // Per-channel DC block + envelope + amp. Partials gating already
            // applied per-mode above; do not re-apply here.
            let left  = leak_dc_ar(left_raw,  0.995) * env * amp;
            let right = leak_dc_ar(right_raw, 0.995) * env * amp;

            [left, right]
        })
});
